[Lang] Add T.reducer_scale for sums rescaled at each step

Online softmax keeps a row sum that is rescaled whenever the running maximum
moves, so flash attention reduced it across threads at every K step: the scale has
to apply to the sum of all threads, and reducers could only accumulate.
Multiplication distributes over the sum, so each thread can scale its own partial
and the sum can be reduced once at the end.

T.reducer_scale(acc[i], factor) does that, on sum reducers only. Its loop must run
on every thread that holds a partial of acc[i]; ReducerPlanAndMaterialize compares
the two thread sets and rejects a mismatch instead of returning a partly scaled
sum. A scale site proposes no plan, so the update sites still choose the layout.

Measured on MI250X, ROCm 7.2.3, same process, 2 rounds: reducing once instead of per
step adds 0 to 4% to flash attention at d128 and d256, depending on tile.

